# work-item-file-dirty.sh golden file — pure decision-logic cases only
# (mode + already-fetched status text -> dirty/clean), transcribed
# verbatim from test-work-item-scripts.sh:1573-1640 per Phase 1 of the
# 0170 implementation plan, not re-derived.
#
# Format: <mode>|<path_relative>|<status_text>|<expected>
# mode is jj|git|none (none = indeterminate). status_text uses the
# script's own injected-override shape: for git, one porcelain line
# (or empty); for jj, the `jj diff --name-only` output containing zero
# or more relative paths, one per line.
#
# The two real-worktree end-to-end cases (committed-clean /
# modified-dirty, exercising the real find_repo_root -> vcs_mode ->
# dispatch chain rather than the injected overrides) are CLI/adapter-
# boundary coverage, not this pure predicate's — see Phase 8's manual
# verification step instead.

git|meta/work/0001-x.md| M meta/work/0001-x.md|dirty
git|meta/work/0001-x.md|(empty)|clean
git|meta/work/0001-x.md|?? meta/work/0001-x.md|dirty
jj|meta/work/0001-x.md|meta/work/0001-x.md|dirty
jj|meta/work/0001-x.md|meta/work/other.md|clean
none|meta/work/0001-x.md|(empty)|dirty
